quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  11,46,"He said: ‘Nuh (Noah)! Indeed, he was not from your family; he had entirely unrighteous conduct. So, do not question Me about things you do not know. I advise you lest you may be among the ignorant.’"
  11,47,"He said: ‘My Lord! I seek Your protection from questioning You about something I do not know. And if You do not forgive me and have mercy upon me, I shall be among the losers.’"
  11,48,"It was said: ‘O Nuh (Noah)! Disembark with peace from Us and blessings upon you and the communities (that will arise) from those with you. And there shall be communities (afterwards) whom We will grant provision, then a painful punishment from Us shall befall them.’"
  11,49,"These are the accounts of the Unseen which We reveal to you. Neither you knew them nor your people before this (revelation). So be patient. Indeed, the ultimate end belongs to the God-conscious."
  11,50,"And to (the people of) ‘Ad, (We sent) their (fellow) brother Hud. He said: ‘O my people! Worship Allah. You have no god other than Him. You are nothing but fabricators (of lies)."
  11,51,O my people! I do not ask for any reward from you. My reward lies only with Him Who originated me. Do you not understand?
  11,52,"O my people! Seek forgiveness from your Lord, then turn to Him in repentance. He will send clouds upon you with abundant rain and add (more) strength to your present strength. So do not turn away, becoming sinners.’"
  11,53,They said: ‘O Hud! You have not brought us any clear proof. We are not going to abandon our gods for your word alone. And we are not going to believe you.
